8. WHATSAPP CLIENT COMMUNICATION

WhatsApp should act as another entry point into the CRM.

Use the official WhatsApp Business Platform.

Do not rely on unofficial automation methods.

8.1 WhatsApp Enquiry Assistant

The chatbot should:

- Welcome new enquiries.
- Understand what the client needs.
- Identify the requested service.
- Collect relevant details.
- Ask for missing information.
- Create or update leads.
- Summarise requirements.
- Preserve conversation history.
- Notify the business owner.

The conversation should feel natural.

Do not make clients answer a long list of questions in a fixed sequence.

The assistant should understand what the client has already explained and ask only for missing information.

8.2 Conversational Onboarding

For simple projects, the chatbot may collect enough information directly.

For complex projects, it should generate a personalised form link.

The form should contain only the information still required.

Do not ask clients to repeat details they have already supplied.

8.3 Human Handover

The business owner must be able to take over a conversation.

When human control is activated:

- The bot must stop responding.
- Incoming messages must remain visible.
- The owner can reply manually.
- The bot stays paused for that client.
- The owner can explicitly return control to the bot.

The system must never allow the bot and owner to respond simultaneously.

8.4 AI Communication Boundaries

The chatbot must not independently:

- Set final prices.
- Approve quotations.
- Negotiate contractual commitments.
- Promise delivery dates.
- Change agreed project scope.
- Confirm payments without verification.
- Make commitments on behalf of the business.

These decisions require human approval.

8.5 AI Cost Management

AI should not be used for every incoming message.

Use ordinary application logic for:

- Greetings.
- Thank-you messages.
- Basic FAQs.
- Simple status retrieval.
- Handover commands.
- Fixed notifications.

Use AI for:

- Understanding complex messages.
- Extracting requirements.
- Summarising conversations.
- Identifying missing information.
- Preparing draft quotations.
- Document extraction.
- Business queries.

Store structured conversation information so the system does not need to send the entire conversation history to the AI provider every time.

Include:

- Configurable AI model.
- API key settings.
- Usage monitoring.
- Token tracking.
- Estimated cost.
- Daily and monthly spending limits.
- Maximum usage per conversation.
- Error handling.
- Manual fallback.

The AI service must be replaceable without rewriting the entire application.

