15. AUTOMATED NOTIFICATIONS AND PAYMENT REMINDERS

The system should handle routine communication automatically.

These automations must run on the backend, not depend on the desktop or Android application being open.

15.1 Payment Reminder System

Provide configurable reminder intervals.

Suggested defaults:

Event| Reminder
Before due date| 5 days before
Due date| On the due date
Overdue| 3 days after
Overdue| 7 days after
Overdue| 14 days after

Allow the owner to change these intervals.

15.2 Reminder Conditions

Before sending a reminder, the system must:

1. Retrieve the invoice.
2. Check whether it has been cancelled.
3. Check whether it has been fully paid.
4. Calculate the current outstanding balance.
5. Check whether the reminder has already been sent.
6. Confirm the communication preference.
7. Send the appropriate message.
8. Record the delivery result.

If a client has made a partial payment, the reminder must reflect the updated outstanding balance.

Do not send reminders for settled invoices.

Prevent duplicate messages.

15.3 Communication Channels

Support:

- WhatsApp.
- Email.
- In-app notifications for the business owner.

Respect client communication preferences and applicable messaging requirements.

Some WhatsApp business messages may require approved templates and incur charges. These costs must be considered when implementing the integration.

15.4 Project Notifications

Notify clients about meaningful events:

- Project started.
- Design ready for review.
- Milestone completed.
- Approval required.
- Revised timeline.
- Delay or important issue.
- Testing completed.
- Deployment completed.
- Project handed over.

Do not notify clients about every internal task.

15.5 Automation History

Every automation should have a record showing:

- Event.
- Trigger.
- Action.
- Recipient.
- Date and time.
- Delivery channel.
- Status.
- Error, if any.
- Retry history.

