24. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

24.1 Recommended Technology Stack

Component| Technology
Android| Kotlin
Desktop| Kotlin + Compose Multiplatform
UI architecture| MVVM
Local database| SQLite / Room
Backend database| Supabase PostgreSQL
Authentication| Supabase Auth
File storage| Supabase Storage
Backend functions| Supabase Edge Functions
Realtime| Supabase Realtime
Push notifications| Firebase Cloud Messaging
Version control| GitHub
Client portal| Responsive web application
AI| Replaceable external AI provider
PDF generation| Dedicated document generation service

The architecture should allow business logic and data models to be shared between Android and desktop where practical.

The client portal should be a separate web interface connected to the same backend.

24.2 Application Architecture

Separate the application into clear layers:

1. Presentation.
2. Application logic.
3. Domain/business logic.
4. Data access.
5. Backend services.

Do not place business rules directly inside UI components.

Use repositories and service classes to separate data access from business logic.

24.3 Offline Support

Android and desktop should support useful offline operations.

Store relevant data locally.

When connectivity returns:

- Synchronise pending changes.
- Resolve conflicts.
- Update records.
- Preserve important transaction history.
- Report failed synchronisation.

Financial operations must have appropriate duplicate prevention and conflict handling.

24.4 Backend-First Automation

Critical business processes must execute on the backend.

Do not rely on the Android app or desktop application remaining open for:

- Payment reminders.
- Project notifications.
- Scheduled follow-ups.
- Maintenance renewal alerts.
- Automation execution.

Use scheduled backend jobs and event processing.

24.5 Multi-Business Readiness

Initially, the system may have one business account.

However, structure the database so that a business or workspace identifier can be added to business records.

This will make future multi-business support easier.

