25.1 Important Database Rules

- Use UUIDs for internal record identifiers.
- Use foreign keys.
- Use appropriate indexes.
- Store timestamps consistently.
- Use explicit status values.
- Use decimal or numeric types for money.
- Preserve historical versions of important records.
- Use soft deletion where records must remain auditable.
- Apply Row Level Security.
- Scope all business data to the correct business.
- Prevent unauthorised access to client information.

The database must not depend on the UI to enforce security.

