30. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

These rules must be implemented consistently.

1. A lead is not automatically a confirmed client.
2. An accepted quotation must be preserved.
3. A project must have a clear agreed scope.
4. Additional work should use change requests.
5. An invoice must not be marked paid without a recorded payment or verified payment confirmation.
6. Partial payments must update the outstanding balance.
7. Fully paid invoices must not receive payment reminders.
8. Payment reminders must use the latest outstanding balance.
9. Project progress must be based on actual milestones or tasks.
10. Clients must only see information approved for them.
11. Internal notes must never appear in the client portal.
12. AI must not independently approve financial or contractual decisions.
13. Important business changes must be auditable.
14. Scheduled automation must run independently of user devices.
15. Duplicate submissions and duplicate automation executions must be prevented.
16. Historical financial and contractual records must be preserved.

